Some minor things:

1) #force shouldn't be limited to chests/boxes.  If you have a club
or iron ball or other large blunt instrument, you ought to be able
to bash doors with it, just as you can with a pickaxe.

2) The rules for time interval between prayers should be clarified
and maybe rationalized.  Perhpas I misread the code, but it looked
like it took a standard quantity like 300 moves, adjusted for luck,
what the god did for you this time, lawful/neutral/chaotic, etc.,
and then multiplied it by some number that was either a small
integer (2-4) or its reciprocal - so it's a random interval,
potentially large, and you have no way to tell whether it's safe to pray.
The old way may have been too deterministic, but this is too random.

3) Priests shouldn't always be Neutral!  If they're always one
alignment, it should be Lawful, though I can accept the concept of
having chaotic priests.  I realize the Priest role-model is more
along the lines of Kung Fu rather than Catholics, but I thought
those guys were kind of Lawful-Neutral rather than Neutral-Good.
Even a Zen Buddhist tend to be Lawful - one's own law rather than
someone else's, but Lawful none the less.  Aren't many True Neutral
role models out there.

4) I get tired of always losing my dogs.  I realize that there are
whistles, and that I have to feed them regularly, but they really
don't follow me around enough.  Maybe I should carry more tripe.

5) Sometimes Elementals are scared off by Elbereth and sometimes
they aren't.  I don't mean that the engraving gets erased, but
rather that they just don't seem to care and hit me anyway.

